      "locked": false,
      "text": "Descriptive Statistics\n1. Define Statistics and what is the need of statistics in machine Learning? [6 Points]\n→ Really impressive answer - https://chat.deepseek.com/share/xhuai5twzu384i0ls7\n\n2. Some theory questions \n    Define the types of statistics\n    Define population and sample also define parameter and statistic?\n\n3. Explain all the sampling techniques\n    Probability sampling 4 and Non probability sampling 4\n\n4. Types of data and there individual sub-types.\n5. What is measure of central tendency and how to measure them?\n    → `mean` gets heavily gets affected by outliers in that case use `median` after sorting the data\n    a. Weighted mean and Trimmed mean - When it is essential to use over Mean?\n\n→ In unimodal moderately skewed destribution (positive and negative), what is the emperical order of mean, median and mode and why\ndoes this happen?\n\n6. What is measure of despersion?\n    a. Define `Range`, `Variance` and `Standard Deviation`? Formulas of variance and std for sample?\n        How do you interprite `std = 0`?\n    b. Define `coefficient of variation` and its usecase?\n        → Scaling increases the variance.\n    c. Define Quantiles, its types and its 2 formulas?\n        a. Difference between percentage and percentile?\n        b. Five Number summary, What does these 5 numbers represent? formula of left and right wiskers. Use of box plot.\n        c. What is IQR and why it is considered as a robust measure dispersion than standard deviation?\n\n7. Univerate, Bivariate and Multivariate analysis ⭐\n    The choice of plots for `num-num`, `num-cat` and `cat-cat` features\n\n",
